is like death and can’t be satisfied, but gathers to himself all nations and heaps to himself all peoples."},{"verse":6,"text":"Won’t all these take up a parable against him, and a taunting proverb against him, and say, ‘Woe to him who increases that which is not his, and who enriches himself by extortion! How long?’"},{"verse":7,"text":"Won’t your debtors rise up suddenly, and wake up those who make you tremble, and you will be their victim?"},{"verse":8,"text":"Because you have plundered many nations, all the remnant of the peoples will plunder you because of men’s blood, and for the violence done to the land, to the city and to all who dwell in it."},{"verse":9,"text":"Woe to him who gets an evil gain for his house, that he may set his nest on high, that he may be delivered from the hand of evil!"},{"verse":10,"text":"You have devised shame to your house by cutting off many peoples, and have sinned against your soul."},{"verse":11,"text":"For the stone will cry out of the wall, and the beam out of the woodwork will answer it."},{"verse":12,"text":"Woe to him who builds a town with blood, and establishes a city by iniquity!"},{"verse":13,"text":"Behold, isn’t it from the LORD of Armies that the peoples labor for the fire, and the nations weary themselves for vanity?"},{"verse":14,"text":"For the earth will be filled with the knowledge of the LORD’s glory, as the waters cover the sea."},{"verse":15,"text":"“Woe to him who gives his neighbor drink, pouring your inflaming wine until they are drunk, so that you may gaze at their naked bodies!"},{"verse":16,"text":"You are filled with shame, and not glory. You will also drink and be exposed! The cup of the LORD’s right hand will come around to you, and disgrace will cover your glory."},{"verse":17,"text":"For the violence done to Lebanon will overwhelm you, and the destruction of the animals will terrify you, because of men’s blood and for the violence done to the land, to every city and to those who dwell in them."},{"verse":18,"text":"“What value does the engraved image have, that its maker has engraved it; the molten image, even the teacher of lies, that he who fashions its form trusts in it, to make mute idols?"},{"verse":19,"text":"Woe to him who says to the wood, ‘Awake!’ or to the mute stone, ‘Arise!’ Shall this teach? Behold, it is overlaid with gold and silver, and there is no breath at all within it."},{"verse":20,"text":"But the LORD is in his holy temple. Let all the earth be silent before him!”"}],"hasArtwork":true,"artworkUrl":"/data/images/books/habakkuk.svg","availableLangs":["zh-CN"]},{"id":"habakkuk_3","bookSlug":"habakkuk","chapter":3,"reference":"Habakkuk 3","title":"Habakkuk 3 — Public Domain Study","topics":["habakkuk","habakkuk","ot","scripture","哈巴谷書","哈巴谷书","哈巴谷的祈禱","哈巴谷的祈祷"],"snippet":{"zh-CN":"先知哈巴谷的祷告，调用流离歌。"},"tokens":{"19":2,"35":1,"habakkuk":10,"public":2,"domain":2,"study":1,"ot":1,"scripture":1,"哈巴谷書":1,"哈巴谷书":2,"哈巴谷的祈禱":1,"哈巴谷的祈祷":1,"先知哈巴谷的祷告":1,"调用流离歌":1,"耶和华啊":3,"我听见你的名声":1,"就惧怕":1,"求你在这些年间复兴你的作为":1,"在这些年间显明出来":1,"在发怒的时候以怜悯为念":1,"神从提幔而来":1,"圣者从巴兰山临到":1,"细拉":6,"他的荣光遮蔽诸天":1,"颂赞充满大地":1,"他的辉煌如同日光":1,"从他手里射出光线":1,"在其中藏着他的能力":1,"在他前面有瘟疫流行":1,"在他脚下有热症发出":1,"他站立":1,"量了大地":1,"观看":2,"赶散万民":1,"永久的山崩裂":1,"长存的岭塌陷":1,"他的作为与古时一样":1,"我见古珊的帐棚遭难":1,"米甸的幔子战兢":1,"你乘在马上":1,"坐在得胜的车上":1,"岂是不喜悦江河":1,"向江河发怒气":1,"向洋海发愤恨吗":1,"你的弓全然显露":1,"向众支派所起的誓都是可信的":1,"你以江河分开大地":1,"山岭见你":1,"无不战惧":1,"大水泛滥过去":1,"深渊发声":1,"汹涌翻腾":1,"因你的箭射出发光":1,"你的枪闪出光耀":1,"日月都在本宫停住":1,"你发忿恨通行大地":1,"发怒气责打列国":1,"如同打粮":1,"你出来要拯救你的百姓":1,"拯救你的受膏者":1,"打破恶人家长的头":1,"露出他的脚":1,"直到颈项":1,"你用敌人的戈矛刺透他战士的头":1,"他们来如旋风":1,"要将我们分散":1,"他们所喜爱的是暗中吞吃贫民":1,"你乘马践踏红海":1,"就是践踏汹涌的大水":1,"我听见耶和华的声音":1,"身体战兢":1,"嘴唇发颤":1,"骨中朽烂":1,"我在所立之处战兢":1,"我只可安静等候灾难之日临到":1,"犯境之民上来":1,"虽然无花果树不发旺":1,"葡萄树不结果":1,"橄榄树也不效力":1,"田地不出粮食":1,"圈中绝了羊":1,"棚内也没有牛":1,"然而":2,"我要因耶和华欢欣":1,"因救我的":1,"神喜乐":1,"主耶和华是我的力量":1,"他使我的脚快如母鹿的蹄":1,"又使我稳行在高处":1,"这歌交与伶长":1,"用丝弦的乐器":1,"belongs":1,"to":5,"the":8,"book":2,"of":5,"old":2,"testament":2,"spanning":1,"chapters":1,"this":